   {
    "category": "fruit",
    "description": "Creamy flesh, a little lime, enough salt. Mash it onto toast or cut it into a bowl of something bright and crunchy. A good avocado hardly needs a recipe.",
    "id": "photo-product-001",
    "name": "Hass avocado"
   },
   {
    "category": "fruit",
    "description": "Dark fruit with a tart edge. Eat a handful before you decide whether the rest belongs in a bowl of yogurt or a warm crumble.",
    "id": "photo-product-098",
    "name": "Blackberries"
   },
   {
    "category": "vegetables",
    "description": "Peppery leaves for a plate that needs an edge. Dress them lightly, or lay them over warm pizza just before it reaches the table.",
    "id": "photo-product-070",
    "name": "Wild Arugula"
   },
   {
    "category": "vegetables",
    "description": "Sharp raw, sweet when cooked. Slice thin for the salad, or let them soften alongside potatoes in the roasting tray.",
